# VPS AI Sysadmin — scheduled routines
# Managed by: docs/infrastructure/vps-ai-sysadmin.md
# Generated by: scripts/bootstrap/bootstrap-vps.sh step_14_install_sysadmin_pack()
# Host: {{HOST_NAME}}  (digest minute slot {{DIGEST_MINUTE}}; keepalive minute slot {{KEEPALIVE_MINUTE}})
#
# Stagger rationale (trio plan r4/r5): all three hosts share one operator
# Claude Code Max account; identical cron times would hit Anthropic's API
# concurrently 3× per fire. Each host's digest + keepalive minute is derived
# from a SHA1 hash of the hostname (modulo 30 and modulo 60 respectively)
# so adding a 4th/5th host later doesn't require touching this file.

# Proactive health check — every 15 min, bash prefilter + Claude on anomaly
*/15 * * * * root /opt/fabrik/scripts/sysadmin/proactive-check.sh >> /var/log/sysadmin-proactive.log 2>&1

# Morning report — daily 08:00, Claude briefing with trends + shift notes
0 8 * * * root /opt/fabrik/scripts/sysadmin/morning-report.sh >> /var/log/sysadmin-proactive.log 2>&1

# Weekly security patrol — Monday 08:30, audit vs security checklist
30 8 * * 1 root /opt/fabrik/scripts/sysadmin/weekly-security.sh >> /var/log/sysadmin-proactive.log 2>&1

# Weekly maintenance — Sunday 03:00, cleanup report (no Claude, pure bash)
0 3 * * 0 root /opt/fabrik/scripts/sysadmin/weekly-maintenance.sh >> /var/log/sysadmin-proactive.log 2>&1

# Monthly backup verification — 1st of month 04:00, backup audit vs checklist
0 4 1 * * root /opt/fabrik/scripts/sysadmin/monthly-backup-verify.sh >> /var/log/sysadmin-proactive.log 2>&1

# OAuth keepalive — hourly (trio plan §2.3 + r3 #22).
# Claude Code OAuth tokens go stale every ~4 days when host is idle (Lesson 75).
# One cheap ping per hour keeps the credentials file fresh. ~$0.005/ping × 24
# = $0.12/host/day on Max subscription burn. Routed through claude-keepalive-rotate.sh,
# which pings via account rotation and writes a CONTENT token (KEEPALIVE_OK /
# KEEPALIVE_FAIL:<reason>) to /var/log/claude-keepalive.log — for daily-digest.sh +
# proactive-check.sh to check (their content-check lands in the monitoring-honesty phase),
# so a real auth/quota break surfaces instead of a perpetually-fresh mtime.
{{KEEPALIVE_MINUTE}} * * * * ozgur /opt/fabrik/scripts/sysadmin/claude-keepalive-rotate.sh > /dev/null 2>&1

# Standby-token refresh — DAILY at 04:{{KEEPALIVE_MINUTE}} (hash-staggered). The keepalive above
# refreshes only the ACTIVE account; the frozen manager-accounts/ SNAPSHOTS go stale (~4-day OAuth
# idle window). This cycles EVERY captured account — switch → bare ping (refresh in place) →
# re-snapshot → restore the original active — so a rotation never lands on a dead standby. Runs as
# ozgur; writes REFRESH_OK / REFRESH_DEAD:<names> to /var/log/claude-refresh-standbys.log (+ a
# best-effort Telegram alert when an account is too dead to refresh — re-capture via claude-manager).
{{KEEPALIVE_MINUTE}} 4 * * * ozgur /opt/fabrik/scripts/sysadmin/claude-refresh-standbys.sh > /dev/null 2>&1

# Daily digest — 09:00 UTC (trio plan §2.8 + r3 #21 + r4 #31).
# Per-host roll-up of Tier A actions / escalations / reverts / consults / health
# heartbeats. Posted to Telegram once per day per host so the operator sees
# a single 3-message digest at 09:00 UTC instead of per-action chatter.
{{DIGEST_MINUTE}} 9 * * * root /opt/fabrik/scripts/sysadmin/daily-digest.sh >> /var/log/sysadmin-proactive.log 2>&1

# Operator-reversal detection — every 5 min (trio plan §5.1.a).
# Correlates AI actions (watchdog sidecar state.db + sysadmin-actions.jsonl)
# against subsequent operator sudo-docker commands within a 5-min window.
# Matches go to /opt/fabrik/logs/lessons-pending.jsonl for weekly review;
# 3+ reversals of the same action class in a week → move that class from
# AUTONOMOUS to ASK OWNER FIRST in system-prompt.txt.
*/5 * * * * root /opt/fabrik/scripts/sysadmin/detect_reversals.py >> /var/log/sysadmin-proactive.log 2>&1
